    "evidence": "Exact diplomatic p179.tex is 4413 bytes, SHA-256 3B4424E98669777F4352A6911DA83D6391DD1412F79FE9C5EE77B8172DB75182. The p180 dip/fr/en proof layers are bound in d1012_source_repair_design.json, 11812 bytes, SHA-256 9F282268F4496469D2601BE25523EF6276F9CF15722D6F50A71B202F32E80B82. Independent review d1012_independent_review_r1.json, 14941 bytes, SHA-256 E8685E081850E1D31ABC93498839FCDB2975DB72BB5972ECC176DEC6BF0C5B55, replays the corrected FR/EN projections, diplomatic invariance, and the exact discharge of D1012-R001. Production resolution additionally requires sealed TOH-P179-COR-002, TOH-SRC-P179-009, and the final D1012 formalization audit.",
    "control": "Preserve the printed self-trace sentence byte-identically in diplomatic French. In corrected French and English use the exact cross-cover quantifier under TOH-P179-COR-002 and TOH-SRC-P179-009. Require the repaired reader and semantic successors plus the final D1012 formalization audit before appending this resolved issue and D001032.",
